  "notes": "Two options exist (Design/Build, Management); built Design/Build as the first-listed, representative pick. New hort_catalog.json (was 2 courses, now 45) and art_catalog.json (was stale/incomplete, now 92 -- ART 20 does exist, the old cached file was just missing it). SPAN 105 and TURF 100 don't exist in the real catalog -- dropped from their pools, leaving SPAN 1/2 and TURF 235 (both real). Several variable-credit bulletin rows resolved to their lower value. CHEM 130 (3cr, no prereq) used instead of CHEM 101 (2cr, needs MATH 21) to avoid one hidden-prereq gap -- but MATH 21 turned out to be needed anyway: ACCTG 211's real prereq is one of MATH 21/110/140, and the bulletin's own required MATH course for this major is MATH 26 (Trigonometry), a genuinely different course that doesn't satisfy it. Added MATH 21 explicitly (Semester 2) rather than leaving ACCTG 211 permanently unschedulable. Post-parens-fix re-scrape revealed MATH 21 itself has a real (previously-hidden) prereq chain: MATH 21 needs MATH 4, which needs MATH 3 -- neither was in the plan, permanently blocking MATH 21 and therefore MATH 26, ACCTG 211, and CHEM 130 downstream. Added MATH 3 (Semester 1) and MATH 4 (Semester 2) explicitly to complete the real chain. Computed total lands at 130cr, above the bulletin's own stated 120-126cr range because of these real, catalog-confirmed additions -- documented, not silently absorbed. PPEM 318 (2cr, no prereq) picked over ENT 313/314, HORT 238, or PPEM 300 for that pool, matching its own 2cr lower bound cleanly. BA 250 (no prereq) picked over BA 304/HORT 455, avoiding HORT 455's own ECON 102/AGBM 101 prereq entirely.",
